  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Removes on.pull_request.paths. Adds an early 'Detect site changes' step that lists the PR's files through the GitHub API (paginated) and writes site=true/false to GITHUB_OUTPUT. The later build/test step is gated on steps.changes.outputs.site == 'true', so the job finishes green on a docs-only PR. Permissions are minimal and the inputs go through env, so there is no injection risk. Minor point: every later step should carry the gate, and there is only one such step, so that is fine. The step depends on gh CLI and API access, which is reasonable on ubuntu-latest. It was not run in CI, and the agent says so."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The diff only touches workflows/ci.yml and stays on the fix. Adding the permissions block and an explanatory comment is a small, justified addition. The agent saw that the file is outside .github/workflows/ and flagged it instead of moving it. No unrelated edits."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 9.0
  },
